## Source review and implementation

- Reviewed Java `NettyRemotingClient.invokeImpl` GO_AWAY handling and `RemotingCommand.createRequestCommand`. Java reconstructs the retry request as a fresh request: code and ext fields/body are carried forward, while the new command gets Java defaults for language/version/flag/remark/opaque and serialization configuration.
- Rust previously cloned the original command, carrying the request flag and remark into retry. Changed GO_AWAY retry to construct a fresh `RemotingCommand` with Java language/default fields, preserving code/ext fields/body. Hooks remain suppressed on retry and the original deadline/admission ownership stays in force.
- Strengthened `p3_go_away_retries_once_on_a_new_connection` to inspect the retried command's Java language, reset flag/remark, preserved ext fields/body, and verify only one outbound hook call.
- Updated README, ADR-0001, Java compatibility summary and Phase 3 inventory to describe tested retry reconstruction and leave ChannelWrapper/reconnect edge behavior marked PARTIAL.
- Full English and Traditional Chinese Phase 3 plans were re-read. No plan edits. Phase 3 remains NOT ACCEPTED; Phase 4 remains blocked. P3-V04 remains deferred to Phase 19.

